00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:04.379
Film Courage: How does the writer know what they are
good at? Writer/Instructor and Script Consultant Shannan E. Johnson (The Professional Pen): Good question.

00:00:04.379 --> 00:00:08.460
I think a lot of that is going to come from
your own confidence. A lot of that is

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:12.089
going to come from
within, just knowing like this

00:00:12.089 --> 00:00:16.350
is a natural skill for me, this is a
natural area for me. But I do think it

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:19.770
takes some time to get there which is
why when writers work with me I will

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:22.890
ask those kinds of questions. Like
are you writing what you'd like to write?

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:26.520
Or are you writing what you like to
watch? Are you writing characters that

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:30.690
you know very well? Or are you writing
characters that you observe? Which is

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:34.649
fine but make sure that if there are
people that you just observe that you

00:00:34.649 --> 00:00:38.010
then try to get in there so you really
know why they do the things that they do

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:42.329
you know and I think a lot of the times
we write what we think is on trend we

00:00:42.329 --> 00:00:46.289
write what we think people are going to
buy and by doing that you're not

00:00:46.289 --> 00:00:50.370
necessarily finding your niche though
you might be finding I don't like this

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:53.789
but the question is are you then gonna
be honest with yourself and say I don't

00:00:53.789 --> 00:00:57.179
like writing this so then you're stop
writing that and start writing what you

00:00:57.179 --> 00:01:01.109
do like so I think it takes some work
but I also think it just takes some

00:01:01.109 --> 00:01:05.520
honesty like within like just just like
it would for anyone who's working any

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:10.260
job there are people who are on their
job right now and they know I don't like

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:15.570
this or they know I have a different
skillset and I do like my job and I had

